-- title:
--   Hecke action on the fppf points sheaf of J⁰
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $N$ be a datum of type `JZeroNeronIdentityComponent p`: a scheme $G$ with a structure morphism $g \colon G \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$, a relative group law $N.L$ on $g$ (functorial multiplication, unit, inverse on $T$-points over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$) that is commutative, a bijection $N.\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_0(p)(\overline{\mathbf Q}) := \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field over $\overline{\mathbf Q}$ onto the $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-points $\{\varphi : \operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbf Q} \to G \mid \varphi \circ g = \text{structure map}\}$ which is additive and Galois-equivariant, a clause providing, for each $t$ in the Hecke algebra $\mathbb T = \mathbf Z[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ acting through `heckeModuleBar p`, an endomorphism of $G$ over $\mathbf Z$ compatible with $N.L$ and inducing $t$ on $\overline{\mathbf Q}$-points, together with the further geometric conditions of the structure (smoothness, separatedness, local finite type, quasi-compactness, surjectivity, preconnected fibres, flatness and surjectivity of multiplication by $n>0$, and finite index of the subgroup generated by the $\mathbf Z$-sections inside the Galois-fixed points), summarised here. Let $\mathcal G$ be a sheaf of abelian groups on the small fppf site of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ (objects: schemes over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ whose structure morphism is flat and locally of finite presentation), and suppose given for each such $U$ a bijection $e_U \colon \mathcal G(U) \to \{\varphi : U \to G \mid \varphi \circ g = U \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z\}$ which carries addition in $\mathcal G(U)$ to the group law $N.L$ on $U$-points, and which is natural: for $k \colon U \to V$ in the site, $e_U(\mathcal G(k)s)$ is $k$ followed by $e_V(s)$. Then there is a ring homomorphism $\rho \colon \mathbb T \to \operatorname{End}\mathcal G$ such that for every $t \in \mathbb T$ there is a single endomorphism $\varphi$ of $G$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ with $N.\mathrm{pts}(t\cdot x)$ equal to $N.\mathrm{pts}(x)$ followed by $\varphi$ for all $x \in J_0(p)(\overline{\mathbf Q})$, and with $e_U(\rho(t)_U s)$ equal to $e_U(s)$ followed by $\varphi$ for every $U$ in the site and every $s \in \mathcal G(U)$.
--
--   This records the action of the Hecke algebra on the identity component of the Néron model of $J_0(p)$ over $\mathbf Z$, transported to any fppf sheaf of abelian groups whose sections are identified additively and naturally with the points of that group scheme; the additivity hypothesis on $e$ is what pins the identification compatibly with $\rho(0)=0$. It feeds the construction of the $p$-primary torsion core of the Néron model used in the study of the Galois module $J_0(p)[\mathfrak m]$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_JZeroNeronIdentityComponent_exists_ringHom_heckeAlg_end_of_sectionsEquiv.lean

